From 11edc017a35c0f7fcd43cc27e16de5552df8edd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:14:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(input): Mod double-right-click toggles maximize

A second Mod+right-click on the same window within the double-click
window (300 ms, 8 px slop) applies the opposite maximize state with a
titlebar double-click's target selection: client_maximize picks the
column or the edges for a tiled window, an unmaximize exits the active
mode first, and a floating window fills the usable area. Clicks past the
window stay single clicks and never toggle.

The pair's first press records the maximize state and defers its resize
grab until the pointer leaves the click's slop: beginResize drops the
layout's maximize bookkeeping (the scrolling layout clears the saved
width fraction at grab start), so a grab on the first press would turn
the second press's restore into a re-maximize. A real drag promotes the
deferred press to a grab before the cursor moves.

Two further properties keep the deferred press safe and precise: the
press snapshots its resize edges, because the thirds zones make the
proposal position-sensitive and the pointer has moved by promotion time
(a press that proposes no edges is a plain click), and view teardown
invalidates the deferred-press and click-pair records through
Cursor::forgetView, since a deferred press holds no grab and the regular
reset paths do not see it.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
